course: dictionary
lesson: 14672
title: Lost in thought
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A long, new word can seem scary, but the words around it give clues. «In his preoccupation, Sam walked straight past the shop and forgot the milk.» Sam was thinking so hard about something else that he missed the shop. So preoccupation means being lost in your own thoughts.
explain: Preoccupation can also mean something that fills your mind all the time. «Football is his main preoccupation.» Football is what Sam thinks about and cares about most. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "Football is his main thing he thinks about" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Notice the phrases that often go with it: «a preoccupation with», «main preoccupation», and «lost in preoccupation». When you see these together, the word becomes easier to remember and to use.
fact: Preoccupation is a noun, so you can write a preoccupation or preoccupations.
fact: «Preoccupation» means a state of thinking about one thing so much that you hardly notice other things.
fact: «Preoccupation» can also mean something that fills your mind all the time, such as a worry or a strong interest.
fact: «Preoccupation with» is followed by the thing someone thinks about, as in «her preoccupation with her homework».
fact: Writers use preoccupation in stories to show a character who is lost in thought or worried.
exercise: «In his preoccupation, Sam walked straight past the shop.» What does preoccupation mean here? | Being very hungry | *Being lost in thought | Running very fast | A kind of shop
exercise: «Football is his main preoccupation.» What does this tell you? | He plays football once a year | He has never seen a football | *Football is what he thinks about most | He hates football
exercise: «Ella's preoccupation was the lost dog, so she barely ate her lunch.» What was Ella's preoccupation? | *The lost dog | The school bell | Her new shoes | Eating her lunch
test: «Lost in preoccupation, the girl did not hear her name being called.» What does lost in preoccupation mean? | Getting lost in a forest | Feeling very cold | *Deep in thought, not noticing things around her | Calling loudly for help
test: Which phrase means something a person cares about most? | a loud whisper | *a main preoccupation | a short sleep | a dark cloud
exam: Mo says «Her preoccupation was her lost cat» means she was happy about her cat. Why is Mo wrong? | Preoccupation means happy | *Preoccupation means a worry or thought that fills the mind, and the lost cat was a worry | Preoccupation means a holiday | Preoccupation means a cat
